### Shared parser reads day-first dates as month-first

The shared parser reads dates month-first. For day-first tenants, that reverses the date. These reports arrived through app, email, and form channels. [Ticket #1](https://github.com/surinderson/mega-dev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) tracks the parser cause; engineering shipped `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` on 5 October.

### Booking-v3 hint conflicts with tenant locale

The booking-v3 form showed `MM/DD/YYYY` to tenants whose locale is day-first, then interpreted the value using that locale. [Ticket #2](https://github.com/surinderson/mega-dev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) tracks this separate cause. The form was retired, so engineering marked it won't fix.

